1. Create `src/context/contentstackContext.tsx` — define a React context that holds Contentstack live preview state (preview token, content type UID, entry UID, live preview hash) and exposes a `useContentstackPreview()` hook; include a `ContentstackProvider` component that initializes state from `window.location` search params and listens for `message` events from the Contentstack preview iframe.

