3. Modify `src/interface/content/page.ts` — add a `ContentstackPreviewState` interface with fields `{ live_preview: string; content_type_uid: string; entry_uid: string }` and an optional `preview` property to the page fetch options type.

4. Modify `src/services/pageService.ts` — update all Contentstack query functions (e.g., `getPage`, `getPages`) to accept an optional `ContentstackPreviewState` parameter and pass it through to the contentstack service so preview params are included in the API request.

5. Modify `src/hooks/useContent.ts` — import `useContentstackPreview` from the new context, pass the current preview state to `pageService` calls, and trigger a data refetch whenever the preview state changes (via `useEffect` dependency on preview hash).

6. Modify `src/pages/_app.tsx` — import `ContentstackProvider` from `src/context/contentstackContext.tsx` and wrap the application component tree with it so all pages and hooks can access preview state.

7. Create `src/components/contentstack/ContentstackQuote/ContentstackQuote.tsx` — implement a presentational component that renders a Contentstack quote block (quote text, author, and optional citation) and accepts `ContentstackAddPreviewButton`-compatible props for inline editing in preview mode.

